  "question": {
    "text": "A straight line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> through the point <math><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> is inclined at an angle of <math><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> to the line <math><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> also intersects the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis, then the equation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi> </mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi> </mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi> </mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> be the slope of the line,</p><p>then <math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> or <math><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> or <math><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math><br /><br />Since L intersects <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis we take <math><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math><br /><br />and get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math><br /><br />Since it passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;therefore line will become <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>"
  }
